From 2bc32d46865247d4dffe8697d491967259b0c8a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Da Bi <isayama@Das-iMac.local>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 14:15:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Fix data race on cell->hydro.sort from the time-step limiter

The time-step limiter self/pair interaction tasks read the sorted arrays
(DOPAIR1 directly; DOSELF1 -> DOSUB_SELF1 via its progeny sub-pairs) but,
unlike the density and force tasks, had no dependency on the hydro sort
task. The sort task runs with lock=0 and, when indices have gone stale,
rewrites the sort buffer in place (cleanup re-sort). With no ordering
between the two, a sort task could overwrite cell->hydro.sort while a
limiter task was iterating it on another thread, yielding half-written
sort indices and an out-of-bounds read on hydro.parts (segfault in
runner_dopair1_branch_limiter).

The earlier deferred-free fix cannot help here: this is an in-place
overwrite of a live buffer, not a use-after-free of a freed one.

Add the hydro.sorts -> t_limiter dependency (ci and, for pairs, cj when
the supers differ), mirroring the density/force tasks. Since no drift
happens between the sorts and the limiter within a step, cells stay
sorted-and-fresh, so no on-the-fly re-sort rewrites the buffer during the
limiter phase and the lock-free reads are safe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014QEuoaGLV1UoeayXpF6SvQ
---
 src/engine_maketasks.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/engine_maketasks.c b/src/engine_maketasks.c
index 3a8bb4e56..a4109cc89 100644
--- a/src/engine_maketasks.c
+++ b/src/engine_maketasks.c
@@ -2666,6 +2666,14 @@ void engine_make_extra_hydroloop_tasks_mapper(void *map_data, int num_elements,
       if (with_timestep_limiter) {
         t_limiter = scheduler_addtask(sched, task_type_self,
                                       task_subtype_limiter, flags, 0, ci, NULL);
+
+        /* The limiter's sub-pair recursion reads the sorted arrays. Make it
+         * depend on the sorts so the sort task cannot rewrite the sort buffer
+         * in place (cleanup re-sort) while the limiter is iterating it. This
+         * is the same dependency the density/force tasks already have; without
+         * it the lock-free limiter reader can pick up half-written sort indices
+         * and do an out-of-bounds read on hydro.parts. */
+        scheduler_addunlock(sched, ci->hydro.super->hydro.sorts, t_limiter);
       }
 
       /* The stellar feedback tasks */
@@ -2975,6 +2983,17 @@ void engine_make_extra_hydroloop_tasks_mapper(void *map_data, int num_elements,
       if (with_timestep_limiter) {
         t_limiter = scheduler_addtask(sched, task_type_pair,
                                       task_subtype_limiter, flags, 0, ci, cj);
+
+        /* The limiter reads the sorted arrays. Make it depend on the sorts so
+         * the sort task cannot rewrite the sort buffer in place (cleanup
+         * re-sort) while the limiter is iterating it. This is the same
+         * dependency the density/force tasks already have; without it the
+         * lock-free limiter reader can pick up half-written sort indices and
+         * do an out-of-bounds read on hydro.parts. */
+        scheduler_addunlock(sched, ci->hydro.super->hydro.sorts, t_limiter);
+        if (ci->hydro.super != cj->hydro.super) {
+          scheduler_addunlock(sched, cj->hydro.super->hydro.sorts, t_limiter);
+        }
       }
 
       /* The stellar feedback tasks */
